#
# Counter-example for the GOVERNING gmeow:AssertedTopologyResultConstraint: a
# gmeow:TopologyComputation asserts a global truth (gmeow:assertsGlobalTruth true) but NO
# gmeow:TopologyClaim discharges it — there is no claim that gmeow:claimForComputation this
# computation, extends its data to a math:GlobalSection, AND discharges the H¹
# math:GluingObstruction. A computed feature is a math:LocalSection, never automatically a
# global truth, so the ∀→∃(join) SPARQL constraint MUST reject it with
# shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent. gmeow:producesResult correctly points at a
# gmeow:TopologyResult wrapper, so the ONLY violation is the undischarged global-truth
# assertion, not a result-object conflation.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/semantic-topology/tests/> .

ex:computationBad a gmeow:TopologyComputation ;
    gmeow:producesResult ex:result ;
    gmeow:assertsGlobalTruth true .               # <-- asserted global truth, no discharging claim

ex:result a gmeow:TopologyResult ;
    gmeow:resultArtifact ex:diagram .

ex:diagram a gmeow:TopologyResult .               # opaque referent stand-in (NOT math-typed)
